quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  57,4,"He is the One Who created the heavens and the earth in six periods, then established His authority on the Throne (i.e. He organised the universe under His Glorious Command). He knows whatever goes deep down into the earth and whatever emerges out of it, and whatever descends from the heaven and whatever ascends to it. He is with you wherever you are. And Allah is All-Seeing of whatever you do."
  57,5,"To Him belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and to Allah, (all) matters are returned."
  57,6,He merges the night into day and merges the day into night. And He is All-Knowing of whatever is (hidden) in the breasts.
  57,7,"Believe in Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and spend out of what He has made you the trustees. Those among you who believe and spend (in Allah’s way) shall have a great reward."
  57,8,Why do you not believe in Allah while (His) Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) calls you to believe in your Lord? He has already taken a pledge from you if you are believers.
  57,9,"He is the One Who sends down clear revelations upon His servant that He may bring you out of utter darkness into light. Indeed, Allah is All-Kind, All-Merciful to you."
  57,10,"Why should you not spend in the way of Allah, while to Allah belongs the heritage of the heavens and the earth? None of you is equal to those who spent (their wealth in the way of Allah) and fought before the victory (of Mecca). They are more exalted in rank than those who spent (their wealth) and fought afterwards. Yet Allah has promised a good reward to all. And Allah is All-Aware of what you do."
  57,11,Who is the one that will lend Allah a good loan so He may multiply it for him? And there will be a generous reward for him.
